WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.500
Let's jump right in.

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:03.400
What is first aid?

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.840
At its simplest, first aid is the immediate care you provide to someone who is injured

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:10.960
or ill before professional help can get to the scene.

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:13.640
First aid can be provided by anyone.

00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:17.360
You don't need a medical degree to make a life-saving difference for someone in need.

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:21.400
Before we get into specific types of injuries or emergencies, let's take a minute

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:25.280
to review the difference between a responsive and unresponsive person.

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:30.840
In a real emergency, you might find yourself helping both responsive and unresponsive people,

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:33.820
and it is important to know the difference between the two.

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:38.360
When we say someone is responsive, it means they are showing clear signs of awareness.

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:42.360
They might be moving around, speaking to you, or even just blinking.

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:46.680
Basically, if you tap them on the shoulder and ask if they are okay, they give you some

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:48.000
kind of reaction.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:52.080
On the other hand, an unresponsive person doesn't show any of those signs.

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:56.520
They won't speak, move, or even blink when you try to get their attention.

00:00:56.520 --> 00:01:01.360
If you encounter someone who is unresponsive, they may need CPR, so your very first step

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:03.840
should always be to call 911 immediately.

